{
  "name": "metta-node",
  "version": "0.0.1-alpha.0",
  "private": true,
  "comment": "Private is this repository's pre-release guard, not a decision about the registry: everything here goes public together on the day the GitHub repository does, and tools/refuse-early-publish.mjs enforces it. The package does carry the engine it mounts; tools/bundle-runtime.mjs copies engine/ and lib/ into _runtime/ on PREPARE, the way the Python package copies them under metta/_runtime at build time. Prepare rather than prepack because prepare is the one hook a consumer installing this DIRECTORY runs: npm's directory fetcher runs prepare and nothing else, so an artefact made only for a pack left `npm install file:...` with a package that had no engine to mount and no browser build to select.",
  "type": "module",
  "description": "MeTTa in TypeScript on the MeTTa Kernel engine, in process over swipl-wasm",
  "license": "MIT",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/MesTTo/MeTTa-Kernel",
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "git+https://github.com/MesTTo/MeTTa-Kernel.git",
    "directory": "extensions/node"
  },
  "sideEffects": false,
